{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The application has failed to provide sufficient information regarding proposed car parking, cycle parking and refuse arrangements for the use. This has therefore resulted in an inadequate assessment regarding provision of these matters which may unacceptably add to parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site. The proposal is considered to have a harmful impact on parking and the highway in the area and therefore considered to be unacceptable and contrary to:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, December 2023)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Policies D5, D6 and T6 of the London Plan (March 2021)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Policies DMT 2, DMT 3, and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;DMSI 8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;of the&amp;nbsp;London Borough of Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;Whilst lacking clarity, the indicative occupancy is considered an over-intensification of the site. T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;he level of activity and comings and goings to the site would be harmful to the neighbouring amenity of surrounding properties.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;The proposal is therefore found to be at odds with the following policies which seek to ensure that development proposals adequately protect residential amenity:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, December 2023)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;Policy D14 of the London Plan (March 2021)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;Policy DMSI 3 and&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14.6667px;&quot;&gt;DMT 2&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;of the&amp;nbsp;London Borough of Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal lacks&amp;nbsp;clarity regarding occupancy numbers. The indicative occupancy is considered&amp;nbsp;an over-intensification of the site, and results in poor&amp;nbsp;quality of accommodation. The proposal is considered unacceptable and contrary to&amp;nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, December 2023), Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021), and Policy DMD 1 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
